==Danish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|da|non|þorp}}, from {{der|da|gem-pro|*þurpą}}, whence also {{cog|de|Dorf}}, {{cog|nds-de|Dörp}}, {{m|nds-de|Dorp}}, {{m|nds-de|Daarp}}, {{cog|nl|dorp}} and {{cog|en|thorp}}.

===Noun===
{{da-noun|en|sg-def-2=torpet|er}} {{attention|da|added headword template, but not sure how to deal with gender}}

# {{lb|da|most commonly}} A solitary [[farm]], distant from other [[settlement]]s.
# A solitary group of farms, distant from other settlements.

==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Etymology===
From {{der|nb|non|þorp}}, from {{der|nb|gem-pro|*þurpą}}, whence also {{cog|de|Dorf}}, {{cog|nds-de|Dörp}}, {{m|nds-de|Dorp}}, {{m|nds-de|Daarp}} and {{cog|nl|dorp}}.

===Noun===
{{nb-noun-n1}}

# {{q|most common}} A solitary [[farm]], distant from other [[settlement]]s.
# {{q|optional}} A solitary group of farms, distant from other settlements.
# {{q|optional before 1960s}} A solitary farm without owned [[land]], renting land from a larger farm nearby.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|nb|torper}}

